Move the command loop's request handling into a CommandScheduler

The command-ordering fix needs the loop's request handling under test,
and that code lived inline in main()'s select loop, where no test could
reach it (only an ignored, device-gated daemon test touched it). This
moves it, unchanged, into CommandScheduler:

- take() is the old branch body: the closed-reply skip, the stopall /
  fadeall generation bump and abort, macro expansion and parsing, the
  32-load limit (now the named MAX_CONCURRENT_LOADS), spawning loads
  that take a permit, and handing ready commands to handle_command with
  the post-command talkback refresh.
- next_load() is the old join branch, pending while no load runs.
- The load semaphore is a constructor argument, so a test can hold a
  load in flight by giving out no permits.
- CommandCtx carries the daemon's start_time so the scheduler can take
  the talkback refresh's timestamp after the command, as the loop did.

The loop builds one CommandCtx per input and calls take(); the test
fixture builds its context through one shared helper and drives the
same scheduler.

Characterization tests pin the existing behaviour before it changes: a
play is answered only once its sample is queued; a missing file is
NotFound, a path outside allowed_directories Forbidden, an unknown
channel InvalidRequest (each logged as "Load failed"); malformed JSON
and unknown commands are InvalidRequest and logged; the 33rd concurrent
load is rejected; stopall cancels a load in flight and one that finished
but was not yet taken (409), and plays sent after a stop start normally;
a request whose client has gone starts nothing, and a loaded play whose
client has gone is discarded; cache commands run as background loads
and stopall cancels them; the scheduler keeps going after a load task
panics; shutdown cancels loads in flight.

Writing them exposed a bug that is fixed separately: a load aborted
before its task first runs drops its HTTP reply instead of answering
409. The tests here yield once so the task is running when the stop
arrives, which is the behaviour they pin.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
and a warning-free release build (RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings); fuzz suite 7
passed; broker-backed native suite (MQTTAUDIO_BROKER_TESTS=1, TLS CA
set) 973 passed, 0 failed, 7 device-gated ignored.

